# Step 1 — Create a Simple Application

Inside your repo, create a folder and cd into it:

mkdir ...
cd ...

Create the following files:
touch app.js package.json Dockerfile


Add the following into app.js:

const express = require("express");

const app = express();

const PORT = 3000;

app.get("/", (req, res) => {
    res.send("Application deployed using GitHub Actions CD Pipeline 🚀");
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
    console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});

Add the following to package.json

{
  "name": "cd-demo",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "app.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node app.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^5.0.0"
  }
}

# Step 2 — Create Dockerfile

Inside the Dockerfile, add the following:


FROM node:20-alpine

WORKDIR /app

COPY package*.json .

RUN npm install

COPY .

EXPOSE 3000

CMD ["npm", "start"]


# Step 3 — Test Docker Locally

In the terminal, input in the following:
docker build -t cd-demo .

Then run:

docker run -p 3000:3000 cd-demo

Test the application on:
http://localhost:3000

You should see: Application deployed using GitHub Actions CD Pipeline 🚀


# Step 4 — Create Docker Hub Repository

Create an account/log in to Docker Hub:

Create a repository for Example: test pipeline


# Step 5 — Create Docker Hub Access Token

Go to: Docker Hub → Account Settings → Personal Access Tokens

Create: New Access Token

Copy the token and username.

# Step 6 — Add GitHub Secrets

Go to your GitHub Repo and then head to:

Settings, Secrets and variables, Actions

Add: Secret 1
Name:DOCKER_USERNAME
Value:your docker username

Add: Secret 2
Name:DOCKER_PASSWORD
Value: your Docker token

# Step 7 — Create CD Workflow

Create:.github/workflows/xxxx.yaml

Add the following into the file:

name: CD Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main


jobs:

  build-and-deploy:

    runs-on: ubuntu-latest


    steps:

      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4


      - name: Login to Docker Hub
        uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          username: ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}
          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKER_PASSWORD }}


      - name: Build Docker image
        run: |
          docker build -t ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}/cd-demo .


      - name: Push Docker image
        run: |
          docker push ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}/cd-demo


      - name: Deploy step
        run: |
          echo "Deployment completed successfully 🚀"


